{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"code-weight-simplify-the-draft-proxy-and-share-its-equality-walker","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code weight: simplify the draft proxy and share its equality walker"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reviewed executable revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"556cbd8ff"},{"type":"text","value":" (base "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"18abceee4"},{"type":"text","value":", the fetched\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":" at review time). This record follows in a documentation-only\ncommit."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a6445a7c2"},{"type":"text","value":" adds the draft revert oracle and the clone and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepEquals"},{"type":"text","value":"\nlaws on unchanged production code."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"639ed5a1e"},{"type":"text","value":" extends the revert oracle after a refactor mutant survived. The\nextension also passes on unchanged code."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"6b68b8dc3"},{"type":"text","value":" is the refactor."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cccaf1b9e"},{"type":"text","value":" returns functions stored in a draft as stored, with a new\nnative-differential law. This is a behavior change and a lost-write fix."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1a07cd3ce"},{"type":"text","value":" applies review fixes: a stronger revert grammar and witness, a\nduplicate comment, and a redundant "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key in"},{"type":"text","value":" check in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getChanges"},{"type":"text","value":" (about 14\nminified bytes)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fcc353d5d"},{"type":"text","value":" through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a49ae90e3"},{"type":"text","value":" fix the bugs that a second review found. Each\nfix extends an oracle first. See Fixes from the second review."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"31b2a6bd4"},{"type":"text","value":" removes draft code that only bought speed. See Code weight over\nspeed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b825e6483"},{"type":"text","value":" fixes a CodeRabbit finding in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineProperty"},{"type":"text","value":" fix: a\nnon-configurable property with an object value threw. See Fixes from the\nsecond review."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0ce101acf"},{"type":"text","value":" fixes two more lost-write classes from CodeRabbit review:\naccessor definitions and typed-array mutator methods."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cbd2aff06"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"556cbd8ff"},{"type":"text","value":" act on a loss audit of these oracles against\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"docs/contributing/oracle-tests.md"},{"type":"text","value":". They fix one bug, make the array and\ntyped-array laws generated, and close the audit's grammar, checkpoint, and\nreplay gaps."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"7e5dfee25"},{"type":"text","value":" fixes three bugs that code review found in the earlier fixes:\nclass write-backs, writes after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.freeze"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subarray"},{"type":"text","value":" reads."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"change","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Change"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/src/proxy.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" builds the drafts that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.update"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withChangeTracking"},{"type":"text","value":" pass to callbacks."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The write-only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxyCache"},{"type":"text","value":", the symbol-key branches over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"assigned_"},{"type":"text","value":", and\nthe one-use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createObjectProxy"},{"type":"text","value":" wrapper are deleted. Every writer of\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"assigned_"},{"type":"text","value":" stores a string key ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"String(prop)"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"String(index)"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"''"},{"type":"text","value":"),\nso the symbol branches could not run."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The custom array iterator is deleted. Arrays bind the native\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array.prototype[Symbol.iterator]"},{"type":"text","value":" to the draft, so each element read takes\nthe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":" trap and its parent edge. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"draft[Symbol.iterator]()"},{"type":"text","value":" now returns a\nnative Array Iterator."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set"},{"type":"text","value":" trap's revert path sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modified"},{"type":"text","value":" and calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"checkParentStatus"},{"type":"text","value":" on\nits own tracker. That function already clears tracking and continues up the\nchain when every value is reverted."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"draftValuesEqual"},{"type":"text","value":" becomes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"draft"},{"type":"text","value":" mode of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepEqualsInternal"},{"type":"text","value":" in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/src/utils.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". Draft mode keeps Map and Set order, RegExp\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"},{"type":"text","value":", and array holes. The general mode does not change."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function stored as data (a field, an array element, a nested object\nmember) is now returned as stored. See Stored functions."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The audit prototype also rewrote "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepClone"},{"type":"text","value":" as one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Reflect.ownKeys"},{"type":"text","value":" loop. That\nloop made every draft 8% to 17% slower, so the refactor first kept the\noriginal two-loop form. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"31b2a6bd4"},{"type":"text","value":" adopts the shorter loop. See Code weight\nover speed."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,"right","right","right"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consumer bundle (esbuild, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"es2020"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"min"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"gzip"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"brotli"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"full public API"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−1,445 (−0.41%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−343 (−0.33%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−108 (−0.12%)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"collection with a filtered live query"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−1,445 (−0.54%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−363 (−0.46%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−279 (−0.41%)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"local-only collection with an insert, an update, and a delete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−1,441 (−1.18%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−350 (−1.00%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−223 (−0.72%)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"local-only collection with one insert"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−1,441 (−1.18%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−350 (−1.00%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−227 (−0.73%)"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each row bundles the built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":", with private members renamed, for base and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"31b2a6bd4"},{"type":"text","value":" under the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":". The refactor alone ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1a07cd3ce"},{"type":"text","value":")\nsaved 1,739 minified and 453 gzip bytes on the full public API. The fixes from\nthe second review added 917 minified and 303 gzip bytes. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"31b2a6bd4"},{"type":"text","value":" then\nremoved 623 minified and 193 gzip bytes of speed-only code."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-the-oracle-work-came-first","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why the oracle work came first"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sixteen source mutants on unchanged code model plausible mistakes in this\nrefactor. Before this work, eight of them passed the whole db suite (7,596\ntests). Seven are real gaps:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A partial revert treated as a full revert, which drops the remaining change\n(P2)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A nested write under a symbol key treated as no change (E5)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepClone"},{"type":"text","value":" copying non-enumerable string keys, or dropping enumerable or\nnon-enumerable symbol keys (C1, C2, C3)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepEquals"},{"type":"text","value":" comparing RegExp "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"},{"type":"text","value":", or treating array holes as\ndifferences (D2, D4)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The eighth, a wrong parent edge for array iterator elements (P4), is\nequivalent under every public observation. See Mutant calibration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A ninth ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepEquals"},{"type":"text","value":" comparing Maps in order) failed one unrelated test only."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"the-draft-revert-oracle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The draft revert oracle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/tests/proxy-revert-oracle.property.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" generates write\nhistories on a draft of a three-field row. An operation sets a field to a new\nvalue, reverts it to its original, deletes it, writes a nested property (a\nstring or symbol key), writes an array index, or writes a row property through\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"for...of"},{"type":"text","value":". Values are primitives (including "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-0"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":"), Dates, RegExps,\nMaps (with primitive or Set values), Sets, arrays with holes, objects with a\nsymbol key, and arrays of rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model applies the same operations to plain-data specs and compares values\nwith its own encoding of draft equality. It never reads a draft. After each\nhistory, the check asserts:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getChanges()"},{"type":"text","value":" holds exactly the fields whose final value differs from the\noriginal, each with that value, and deleted fields as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The draft reads back the model's final value."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The original row is unchanged."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The generator also emits a revert of a field that is currently changed, so\nmost reverts run the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set"},{"type":"text","value":" trap's revert branch. A second property builds\npartial reverts directly: it changes two or three fields in any order, then\nreverts all of them but one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each property runs a fixed campaign (seed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2026101"},{"type":"text","value":") and a random campaign:\n400 general histories and 200 partial-revert histories.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TANSTACK_DB_PROXY_REVERT_SEED"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TANSTACK_DB_PROXY_REVERT_PATH"},{"type":"text","value":" select a\nreplay. A positive witness requires the fixed general campaign to reach every\noperation, a change made only under a nested symbol key, and effective\nreverts: at least 10 histories where a change survives a revert, and at least\n30 histories that end fully reverted. A revert counts only when the field\ndiffers from its original before the revert. Eleven pinned histories hold one\nrule each."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review of the first version found that its witness also counted reverts of\nunchanged fields, which write an equal value and do nothing. With those\nexcluded, the first grammar reached 10 partial and 11 full reverts in 400\nhistories. The changed-field revert and the partial-revert property raise\nthat coverage. Mutant N2 now fails 6 of the oracle's 16 cases, including both\npartial-revert campaigns."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Map, Set, and array mutator methods ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"add"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"push"},{"type":"text","value":") mark a value\nchanged without a revert check. The native-operation tests in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" own them."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Top-level symbol writes are outside the grammar. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getChanges()"},{"type":"text","value":" does not\nreport them, and the coverage map lists symbol writes as unsupported."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"clone-key-classes-and-deepequals-order-rules","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clone key classes and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepEquals"},{"type":"text","value":" order rules"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy-detachment-contract.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" pins that a draft copies a row's own\nenumerable string keys and every own symbol key, enumerable or not, and\ndoes not copy non-enumerable string keys. This is current behavior, not a\npromise."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"utils.property.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" adds four generated laws: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepEquals"},{"type":"text","value":" ignores Map\nand Set insertion order, RegExp "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"},{"type":"text","value":", and array holes. These are the\nrules draft equality keeps, so a shared walker must not leak one mode into\nthe other."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"stored-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stored functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":" trap bound every function it returned to the private copy, so it\ncould call built-in methods such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Map.prototype.get"},{"type":"text","value":", which reject a Proxy\nreceiver. That binding also applied to functions stored as data:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read on a draft of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ handler: f, fns: [f], obj: { g: f } }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"refactor before the fix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"now"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"draft.handler === f"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"true"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"draft.fns[0] === f"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"true"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[...draft.fns][0] === f"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"for...of"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"true"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"draft.obj.g === f"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"true"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":", array iteration was the only read path that kept identity, because\nthe custom array iterator did not take the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":" trap. The native iterator\ndoes, so the refactor first lost identity there too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The binding had a worse effect: a stored method saw the private copy as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":".\nA method such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bump() { this.count++ }"},{"type":"text","value":" then changed the copy without\ntracking, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getChanges()"},{"type":"text","value":" reported no change. Inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.update"},{"type":"text","value":",\nthat write was lost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cccaf1b9e"},{"type":"text","value":" returns an own data function as stored. A call then sees the draft\nas "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":", so its writes take the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set"},{"type":"text","value":" trap. Inherited Array, Map, and Set\nmethods keep their draft handling."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" adds a native-differential law. Each probe runs on a native row\nand on a draft of an equal row, and the results must be equal. The probes are\nfield access, array index, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"for...of"},{"type":"text","value":", spread, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"includes"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"indexOf"},{"type":"text","value":", an\narray callback, a nested field, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.values"},{"type":"text","value":", a Map value, a Set member, a\ncall, a function assigned during the callback, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":" inside a stored\nmethod. One more case checks that a write through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":" appears in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getChanges()"},{"type":"text","value":". The law fails 8 of 14 cases on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" and 10 of 14 on the\nrefactor before the fix."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cccaf1b9e"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owners"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"F1: every function is bound again"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (10/455)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"F2: inherited methods are returned unbound too"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (103/455)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"F3: the own-property check reads the original row"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (1/455)"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"fixes-from-the-second-review","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fixes from the second review"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A second review found one regression in the refactor and several bugs that\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" also has. Each fix extends an owner first, so the new law fails before\nthe fix. Bytes are for the full public API, minified and gzip, against the\ncommit before."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null,"right"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commit"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bug"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owner law"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fails on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bytes"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fcc353d5d"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A nested add-then-delete, a fully reverted nested object beside a changed sibling, and a key added as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" left wrong changes."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Revert oracle: nested delete op and nested round-trip property."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6 of 24 cases"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"+138 / +49"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"36030ef8f"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The refactor cloned a typed array with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"new Ctor(source)"},{"type":"text","value":", so a subclass that does not forward its argument cloned empty. A typed array of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":" never equaled itself."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Revert oracle: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Float64Array"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Uint8Array"},{"type":"text","value":", and a subclass, with index writes. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"utils.property"},{"type":"text","value":": typed elements compare like numbers."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NaN cases only"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"+133 / +53"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"967a28c1d"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The native iterator bound to the draft made "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"for...of"},{"type":"text","value":" over 200 numbers 4 times slower than "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Iteration contract: arrays visit and publish what a native array does, with an edit while the iterator is open."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none (performance)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"+293 / +93"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"5b4049cdf"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"General mode allocated a draft entry list for every Map."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing Map mutants N6, N11, N14."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none (performance)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−5 / +5"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b57d60022"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"at"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"slice"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"concat"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flat"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toReversed"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toSpliced"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"with"},{"type":"text","value":" returned raw elements, so a write through them was lost. A search for a draft element failed, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"constructor"},{"type":"text","value":" was a bound copy."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":": every non-mutating method of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array.prototype"},{"type":"text","value":", against a native array."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"15 of 39 cases"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"+38 / +16"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"38d8ba78f"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.defineProperty(draft, key, { value })"},{"type":"text","value":" threw unless the descriptor set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"writable"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":": six definitions against a native row."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3 of 6 cases"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"+8 / +8"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"815432ebd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two URLs, or two instances whose state is in private fields, were equal, so a draft dropped a write that replaced one."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Revert oracle: URL values and a private-field class, with a write-twice property. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"utils.property"},{"type":"text","value":": class and identity law."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"both campaigns"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"+312 / +79"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b825e6483"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"38d8ba78f"},{"type":"text","value":" defined a clone, so a non-configurable object value broke the Proxy invariants and threw. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":" would also have wrapped it."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineProperty"},{"type":"text","value":" law: a new key with only an object value, with identity where the invariants require it."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"throws on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" too"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"+9 / +5 (module only)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0ce101acf"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defining a getter over a field reported no change. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sort"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reverse"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"copyWithin"},{"type":"text","value":", and writes through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subarray"},{"type":"text","value":" on a typed-array draft changed the private copy without a change."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":": every method of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TypedArray.prototype"},{"type":"text","value":" against a native typed array, and two getter definitions."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6 of 31 methods, 2 of 2 getters"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"+70 / +25 (module only)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"7e5dfee25"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The class rule made writing back the row's own class instance a change, because draft snapshots hold class instances as plain objects. After "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.freeze(draft)"},{"type":"text","value":", a nested write was lost. A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subarray"},{"type":"text","value":" read counted as a change."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Revert oracle: a keyed class instance in original rows. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":": rows after freeze, seal, or a fixed key against native rows, and the typed-array law with and without a write."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7 oracle cases and 3 pinned cases on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ca0a2170c"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"about +160 / — (proxy and utils modules)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cbd2aff06"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sort"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reverse"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"copyWithin"},{"type":"text","value":" on a draft returned the private copy, not the draft. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" has the same bug."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"N: generated rows record whether a method returned the array itself."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the four self-returning mutators, on arrays and typed arrays"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"small (one comparison)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"556cbd8ff"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No product bug. R's grammar could not write back the row's own object, the frozen-key boundary had no nearby witness, and the two-step callback property had no fixed campaign or replay."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"R: same-object reverts. T: sealed and read-only configurable keys. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":": campaigns and replay."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"F4 survived before the read-only configurable case"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"0"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a49ae90e3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None. A detached stored method must throw, as on a native row."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" stored-function law."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"passes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"0"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Design decisions for these fixes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed-array class."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Draft equality treats a typed array of another class\nas a change. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deepEquals"},{"type":"text","value":" still ignores the class, as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"utils.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" has\npinned since #434."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array read methods."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Every non-mutating method reads through the draft.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b57d60022"},{"type":"text","value":" first ran searches, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"join"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keys"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toString"},{"type":"text","value":" on the copy\nfor speed. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"31b2a6bd4"},{"type":"text","value":" removed that list. Running the element methods on the\ncopy and then replacing elements with drafts was faster but cost 167 more\ngzip bytes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Classes and keyless objects."}]},{"type":"text","value":" In both modes, instances of two different\nclasses differ. A plain or null-prototype object from any realm compares by\nkeys with any class, because draft snapshots and plain JSON hold class\ninstances as plain objects. ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"815432ebd"},{"type":"text","value":" first made a plain object differ\nfrom a class instance; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"7e5dfee25"},{"type":"text","value":" reverted that after review found that\nwriting back the row's own instance became a change.)\nA class instance without enumerable keys equals only itself. URLs compare\nby "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"href"},{"type":"text","value":", because a draft copies a URL by its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"href"},{"type":"text","value":"; by identity, an\nuntouched URL would differ from its own snapshot."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The law that takes its methods from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array.prototype"},{"type":"text","value":" closes a whole class: a\nnew built-in method fails the law until it has arguments. Its last case also\ncaught the bound "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"constructor"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits that remain:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A draft reads a class instance of the original row as a plain object, so a\nprivate-field getter reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":". The detachment contract owns that\nboundary. The revert oracle writes class instances but never starts with\none."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A built-in method called through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":" on a nested Map or Set draft, such\nas "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Map.prototype.get.call(this.m, key)"},{"type":"text","value":", throws, because the receiver is a\nProxy. This is a Proxy limit."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reading an object under a frozen or fixed key of a draft counts that key as\nchanged, because the Proxy invariants require the raw copy. The row may\npublish an equal value."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Writing back a keyless class instance of the original row counts as a\nchange, because the snapshot holds it as an empty plain object."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DataView"},{"type":"text","value":" setters on a draft are not tracked. No owner generates a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DataView"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A mutator method that changes nothing, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sort"},{"type":"text","value":" on a sorted array or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"add"},{"type":"text","value":" of a present Set member, counts as a change, so the row publishes an\nequal value. Arrays, Maps, and Sets did this on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":". Typed arrays do too\nsince "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0ce101acf"},{"type":"text","value":". This is a deliberate limit: a revert check after mutators\nwould cost bytes to avoid a publish of an equal value."}]}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owners"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T1: typed clone by constructor argument"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (7/470)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T2: typed elements compare with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"!=="}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (9/470)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T3: draft ignores typed-array class"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (1/470)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I1: iterator yields raw elements"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (9/488)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I2: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"entries()"},{"type":"text","value":" yields no index"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (7/488)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I3: iterator records a wrong parent edge"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (19/488)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I4: iterator caches the length"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (12/488)"}]}